# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Unknown paths used to answer 200 with a byte-for-byte copy of the home
# page: /nope-404, /robots.txt and /sitemap.xml all looked like they had
# worked. Search engines index those duplicates, and a mistyped link reads
# as a live page instead of a mistake.
#
# Cloudflare Pages serves a real file first and only falls through to this
# list when nothing matches — so /assets/app.js still comes from disk and
# never enters here. Anything left over is a path the site does not have,
# and the home page is the honest answer: this is a one-page site with a
# menu, a map link and a phone number, not a set of separate pages.
#
# 301 so a search engine stops treating the wrong URL as a distinct page.
# Copied into the build output by build.sh, like _headers.

/*    /    301
